      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "The Vyper compiler vulnerability exploited in the Curve hack was buried in release history — standard pre-release audits rarely examine version-specific compiler changelogs, leaving a structurally blind spot at every upgrade.",
          "source": "https://www.adevarlabs.com/blog/the-defi-pre-launch-security-checklist-2026-edition"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Concurrent releases from US Treasury, IOSCO, and BIS in 2024–2025 signal coordinated multi-jurisdiction rulemaking that could reclassify DeFi yield products and stability pools as securities or deposits.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Liquidity",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Token unlocks at mainnet launch or TGE create predictable sell pressure; analysis of 16,000+ unlocks shows cliff events routinely suppress price 20–40% in the surrounding window.",
          "source": "https://keyrock.com/from-locked-to-liquidity-what-16000-token-unlocks-teach-us/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Pre-launch hype can structurally decouple from post-release utility — Solana's phone hit $70M in preorders yet sold through slowly, illustrating demand that evaporates once the release date is known.",
          "source": ""
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "Low",
          "note": "Open-source release of codebases (Paradigm Rivet, Monad docs, LegibleMath whitepaper) distributes technical knowledge and reduces single-team dependency risk, though release timing still concentrates information advantage.",
          "source": "https://mbrenndoerfer.com/writing/responsible-deployment-staged-release-access-control-monitoring"
        }
